---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import { HardDrive, EyeOff, Network, Database, ShieldCheck } from '@lucide/astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Macmo approaches privacy: local-first architecture, no mandatory cloud backend, local-only IPC, secure credential storage, and no required telemetry."
  canonical="https://macmo.anakterubuk.tech/privacy"
>
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <SectionHeading
        kicker="Privacy"
        title="Local-first by design."
        body="This page describes how Macmo approaches privacy and security during V1 development. It reflects the product requirements defined in the Macmo V1 PRD and may change as the product evolves."
        reference="Based on PRD §22 Security · §23 Privacy"
        level="h1"
      />

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-card bg-surface p-6 hairline">
          <HardDrive class="size-5 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">Default model</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-sm text-text-muted">
            Your Agents <span class="text-text-faint">↓</span><br />
            Your Mac <span class="text-text-faint">↓</span><br />
            Macmo
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
            Macmo V1 is designed so the core product does not depend on a cloud
            service. There is no mandatory cloud backend, accounts, or
            synchronization in V1.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card bg-surface p-6 hairline">
          <EyeOff class="size-5 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">Telemetry</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
            Macmo V1 does not require telemetry. If telemetry is ever
            introduced, it is specified to be opt-in, documented, minimal, and
            configurable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card bg-surface p-6 hairline">
          <Network class="size-5 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">Local communication</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-sm text-text-muted">
            <li>Local-only inter-process communication over Unix Domain Sockets</li>
            <li>No public network exposure for the IPC layer</li>
            <li>Event schema and payload validation</li>
            <li>Malformed events are rejected</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card bg-surface p-6 hairline">
          <Database class="size-5 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">Data on your Mac</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-sm text-text-muted">
            <li>SQLite stores local application state</li>
            <li>Credentials are stored in the macOS Keychain</li>
            <li>SQLite does not replace secure credential storage</li>
            <li>Permission decisions are logged locally</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-card bg-surface p-6 hairline lg:col-span-2">
          <ShieldCheck class="size-5 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">Security principles</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2.5 text-sm text-text-muted sm:grid-cols-2">
            <li>Local-first</li>
            <li>Least privilege</li>
            <li>No unnecessary network listeners</li>
            <li>Secure credential storage</li>
            <li>Explicit permissions</li>
            <li>Event validation</li>
            <li>Audit logging</li>
            <li>Human-controlled approvals</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="micro-note mt-6 text-text-faint">
            Macmo is in early development. Nothing on this site is a legal
            guarantee or a claim of certification.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
